# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# Every path serves the app, because routing happens in the browser: /review is a
# Blazor route, not a file. The 200 matters — a 302 to / would lose the path the
# visitor asked for, so a shared link to a step would always land on step one.
#
# App.razor renders its own "No such page" for anything it does not recognise, so an
# unknown path is answered by the app rather than by Cloudflare. Assets that do exist
# on disk are served before this rule is consulted.
/*    /index.html   200
